  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "SD-001",
      "title": "CLOBTransferHandler ammHandleTransfer Missing FOT Balance Check Creates Maker Insolvency",
      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence": "high",
      "confidence_score": 85,
      "confidence_deductions": [
        {
          "deduction": -5,
          "reason": "Requires FOT token as pool tokenOut \u2014 depends on pool creator's token choice"
        },
        {
          "deduction": -10,
          "reason": "PoC demonstrates accounting gap but uses direct storage manipulation rather than full AMM flow"
        }
      ],
      "contracts": [
        "CLOBTransferHandler"
      ],
      "functions": [
        "ammHandleTransfer",
        "depositToken",
        "withdrawToken"
      ],
      "description": "The CLOBTransferHandler.depositToken() function (lines 362-369) correctly checks for fee-on-transfer (FOT) tokens by comparing balanceOf before and after the transfer, reverting with CLOBTransferHandler__InvalidTransferAmount if they don't match. However, the ammHandleTransfer() function (lines 221-300) has NO such check when the AMM sends tokenOut to the handler after filling CLOB orders.\n\nDuring ammHandleTransfer:\n1. CLOBHelper.fillOrder() credits maker virtual balances with the full amountOut (line 234: makerTokenBalance[maker] += stepOutput)\n2. Handler sends tokenIn to AMM (line 296)\n3. AMM later sends tokenOut to handler (AMMModule.sol line 2239)\n4. If tokenOut is a FOT token, handler receives amountOut - fee\n5. Total virtual balance > actual handler balance = INSOLVENCY\n\nVictim: The last maker(s) to withdraw cannot retrieve their full balance because the handler's actual token balance is less than the sum of all virtual balances.\n\nEconomic impact: deficit = FOT_fee_rate \u00d7 amountOut per swap. With 5% FOT and 1000 token swap, deficit = 50 tokens. Compounds with each swap through the CLOB.",
      "poc_file": "lbamm-hooks-and-handlers/test/AuditStateDesyncCLOB.t.sol",
      "poc_tests": [
        "test_H15_depositToken_rejects_FOT",
        "test_H15_FOT_creates_virtual_balance_desync",
        "test_H15_last_maker_cannot_withdraw"
      ],
      "fp_gate": {
        "location_exists": true,
        "entry_reachable": true,
        "no_existing_guard": true,
        "concrete_attack_path": true,
        "poc_compiles": true
      },
      "attack_sequence": [
        "1. Pool created with normal tokenIn and FOT tokenOut",
        "2. Makers deposit tokenIn, open orders on CLOB",
        "3. Executor swaps tokenIn -> tokenOut through AMM with CLOB handler",
        "4. ammHandleTransfer fills orders: makers credited full amountOut",
        "5. AMM safeTransfers tokenOut to handler: handler receives amountOut - FOT_fee",
        "6. Virtual balances (1000) > actual balance (950) for 5% FOT",
        "7. First maker withdraws 500 -> succeeds (handler has 950)",
        "8. Second maker tries to withdraw 500 -> FAILS (handler has 450)"
      ],
      "root_cause": "Asymmetric FOT protection: depositToken checks balance before/after (line 362-369), but ammHandleTransfer does not check received tokenOut amount from AMM",
      "references": [
        "CLOBTransferHandler.sol:221-300 (ammHandleTransfer - no FOT check)",
        "CLOBTransferHandler.sol:354-375 (depositToken - has FOT check)",
        "CLOBHelper.sol:180-239 (fillOrder - credits makers at line 234)",
        "AMMModule.sol:2235-2244 (AMM sends tokenOut to recipient)"
      ],
      "kill_gate": {
        "status": "flagged",
        "gate": "V2-refutation",
        "reason": "Missing refutation_attempted \u2014 you must argue against your own finding before submitting"
      }
    }
  ],
